{title: O How I Love Jesus}
{key: G}
{x_theme: blood}
{x_source: chrd:o_how_i_love_jesus.chrd}

{comment: Verse 1}
[G]There is a name I love to hear, I [D]love to sing its [G]worth.
[G]It sounds like music in my ear, the [D]sweetest name on [G]earth.

{comment: Chorus}
[G]O, how I love Jesus, [D]O, how I love Je[G]sus,
[G]O, how I love Jesus, be[D]cause He first loved [G]me!

{comment: Verse 2}
[G]It tells me of a Savior's love, who [D]died to set me [G]free.
[G]It tells me of His precious blood, the [D]sinner's perfect [G]plea.

{comment: Verse 3}
[G]It tells me what my Father hath in [D]store for ev'ry [G]day,
[G]And, though I tread a dark-some path, yields sun[D]shine all the [G]way.

{comment: Verse 4}
[G]It tells of One whose loving heart can [D]feel my deepest [G]woe,
[G]Who in each sorrow bears a part that [D]none can bear [G]below.
